      "body": "**TLDR:** `_local_reorder` sorts expert ids as int16 when `num_experts` fits: 2 radix passes instead of 8, same permutation.\n\n**Problem**\n1. **Sort today.** `_local_reorder` sorts top-k expert ids as int64.\n2. **Radix sort.** CUDA's radix sort runs one pass per 8 key bits: 8 passes for int64.\n3. **Cost.** Sort 72.9 us at 4k x 8 ids.\n\n**Solution**\n1. **int16 keys** when `num_experts` fits: 2 passes.\n2. **Unchanged.** The stable permutation is identical; the guard is on a Python int, so no new graphs.\n\n**Results**\n```text\nsort, 4k x 8 ids: 72.9 -> 30.4 us   (~40 us per MoE layer; measured on an earlier tree)\nDSv3 671B layers 2-3, flex attention, fwd+bwd wall, 1x GB300 (shared), median [range] of 3 fresh processes, no AC\n16k   159.76 [159.67-159.78] -> 159.74 [159.39-160.19] ms   (within noise)\ncorrectness: bitwise\n```\n\nNOTE:\n- Below the 1% bar; kept because it is 4 lines and bitwise.\n- Reaches Local, AllToAll and TorchAO dispatchers of every MoE model, eager and compiled.\n- Not tested: H100; backward recompute under AC.\n\n**Test plan**\n`pytest tests/unit_tests/cpu/test_token_dispatcher_compile.py -k test_local_reorder_matches_int64_expert_sort` (896 experts: ids need > 8 bits)\n\n<details><summary>Stack summary (same in every PR)</summary>\n\n```text\nDeepSeek-V3 671B layers 2 (dense) + 3 (MoE), native dims, 128 local experts (one EP2 rank), local dispatcher\nflex attention, fwd+bwd wall, 1x GB300 (shared), upstream main 2154d68a9, median of 3 fresh processes\n\nupstream regions -> stack   16k no AC   184.49 -> 159.58 ms  (-13.5%)\n  with fused_mla instead of mla_qk      184.49 -> 156.24 ms  (-15.3%)\nEP>1 only (op level): EP permutes -5.3 ms per MoE layer at 16k\n\nstack (biggest first; per-PR deltas measured one base earlier, same code)\n1 moe_dispatch_combine      -6.4%\n2 mla_qk                    -7.5%\n3 EP permute gathers        EP>1 only\n4 router region             -0.2% (EP2 width; -0.65 ms per MoE layer at 256 experts)\n5 int16 sort keys           within noise (bitwise, 4 lines)   <- this PR\nMade with the local_compile_perf skill: https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/pull/5155\n```\n</details>\n\nStack: 5 of 5.\n",
      "changedFiles": 2,
